 "title": "Chemical and Organism Interactions in Chemostats",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the interactions between various chemicals and organisms in chemostat vessels. The organism A-L+ has affinity for hypoxanthine and is in chemostats, while L-A+ grows in SD and has hypoxanthine. CoSMO is consumed by hypoxanthine and has consumption relationships with A-L+ and L-A+. The chemostat process involves CoSMO, and flow cytometry is a process for A-L+. The cluster also includes various chemical and organism relationships, such as the consumption of lysine by CoSMO and L-A+, and the release of GSH by WY1335 and lys-.",
